title: 'provider flag conflates TTS and STT: minimax TTS cannot pair with the configured default STT in ask / tts --listen'
updated_at: "2026-08-23T08:10:58Z"
---
GitHub: https://github.com/ultradyn/hark/issues/10

What happens: `hark ask --provider minimax "..."` and `hark tts --provider minimax --listen "..."` play the TTS fine, then fail the listen leg with "minimax STT unsupported (no stable public ASR in v1); use xai|openai|google". The single --provider flag is applied to BOTH legs.

Impact: MiniMax is TTS-only, so it can never be used with ask / tts --listen even though config has a perfectly good default STT (custom grok-stt endpoint). In the filing session Google TTS was rejecting question-shaped text (see B177 / gh-9), so minimax TTS + default STT was exactly the combination needed. The only workaround was two commands (hark tts --provider minimax "Q" && hark listen), which loses ask confirm/meta-command handling and event tagging.

Current state verified 2026-08-23: still unfixed. src/hark/cli.py has a bare --provider on tts (:284), listen (:323) and ask (:349); there are no --tts-provider / --stt-provider flags anywhere.

Expected: separate --tts-provider / --stt-provider flags, OR --provider applies to TTS only while STT uses its configured provider. STT provider selection already exists independently in config.

DESIGN DECISION (coordinator, 2026-08-23): add explicit --tts-provider / --stt-provider, and keep --provider as a both-legs shorthand for backwards compatibility. Rationale: silently narrowing --provider to TTS-only would change the meaning of existing invocations without an error, which is worse than a new flag. Where --provider is given alongside a specific flag, the specific flag wins; say so in --help.
On `listen` (STT-only) --provider and --stt-provider mean the same thing - do not error on the pair.

Sequencing: land this BEFORE B177/gh-9 (TTS fallback). Both touch provider resolution; doing selection first gives the fallback work a clean per-leg provider to fall back within.

Version at filing: 2026-08-17, editable v0.1.0, git v0.1.10-324-g9ea9549-dirty.

Audit 2026-10-26: already fixed on current master; no new implementation needed. Independent TTS/STT leg selection, CLI flags and confirmation/nudge routing remain wired; tests/test_provider_legs.py. Inspected whole ticket, code and regressions; final combined remote suite will validate integration.